# Importing from Lovable

Lovable owns the design language. When importing, **keep their visual choices** (colors, spacing, layout, component structure). Only apply our technical infrastructure.

## What to convert (technical only)

### Breakpoints → container queries
| Lovable | Falak |
|---------|-------|
| `sm:` | remove or `@md:` |
| `md:` | `@md:` (640px container) |
| `lg:` / `xl:` / `2xl:` | `@lg:` (896px container) |

### Hardcoded sizes → tokens
| Lovable | Falak |
|---------|-------|
| `h-8` / `h-9` / `h-10` on inputs | `h-input` |
| `w-8 h-8` / `w-10 h-10` on icon buttons | `w-icon-btn h-icon-btn` |
| `w-4 h-4` on icons in buttons | `w-icon-sm h-icon-sm` |
| `w-5 h-5` on icons | `w-icon-md h-icon-md` |

### Container setup
- Add `style={{ containerType: "inline-size" }}` to layout wrappers
- Add `cq-adapt` to cards that need container-responsive sizing

## What to keep from Lovable
- Colors, gradients, shadows
- Spacing values, padding, gaps
- Border radius, opacity
- Component structure and hierarchy
- Animations and transitions
- Typography choices (convert to nearest token: text-label/text-sub/text-body/text-heading)
- Layout patterns, grid structures

## What to wire up
- Replace mock data with server actions from `src/actions/`
- Replace Lovable's routing with Next.js App Router
- Use existing shared components where they exist (`data-table`, `action-menu`, `related-table`)
- Integrate Clerk auth where needed
